  "notes": [
    "Host authoring references only. Definitions have no effect on runtime laws, propagation, delay or interaction strengths.",
    "A constant may be chosen as a unit: one value in planck_h is one Planck constant of action; one value in speed_of_light is one physical vacuum light speed. These are dimensionally different quantities.",
    "Model h is a time interval, not Planck action. The opt-in Node profile uses k local h steps followed by one hop; other profiles retain configured link_ticks and cost-budget timing. No SI tick duration is assigned here.",
    "Physical link speed needs an explicit length per Link and time per tick calibration plus link_ticks. No equality of a candidate field propagation speed and physical c is inferred.",
    "Finite decimal measurements are selected central values. Conversion uses their exact written ratios; experimental uncertainty, correlations and model error remain separate from component encoding error.",
    "There is no asserted universal integer rest-mass quantum. A field scale is an explicit representation choice. All three vector components share its unit and scale.",
    "No finite rational hbar is labeled exact: hbar=h/(2*pi) requires an explicitly controlled approximation if a future authoring model uses it.",
    "The SI dimension ordering is compatible with the proposed si-rational-v1 authoring convention in PR56; this registry does not activate that unmerged runtime interface."
  ]
